  "interpretation_guardrail": "Faint-vector and paper masks are acting-safe measurement probes, not truth. A useful enhancement must improve coherent target strokes without proportionally increasing paper selection or deleting reliable full-page anchor ink.",
  "post_run_visual_review": {
    "decision": "promote_source_only_reconnect_3x7_as_bounded_preprocessing_candidate",
    "frozen_before_sealed_evaluation": false,
    "meaning": "Strengthening only weak Eynollah-supported source fragments produced the best balanced result on this crop. At p0.50 faint-proxy recall rose from 34.77% to 52.17%, full-page anchor retention rose from 90.65% to 96.00%, paper-proxy selection remained zero, and components fell from 54 to 38. This demonstrates improved faint-ink visibility, not single-word ownership: neighboring fragments remain visible at crop edges and must be separated later by line and word ownership.",
    "synthetic_bridge_finding": "Reject both temporary-bridge variants. After selected synthetic pixels were removed, tight 3x7 retained 9040 source pixels in 40 components and broad 5x11 retained 8612 in 46, both worse than source-only reconnect at 9529 pixels in 38 components. Artificial continuity did not help Eynollah recover more exact source ink.",
    "sealed_human_evidence_inspected": false
  },
